WEBVTT

00:04.120 --> 00:08.610
<i>There are more first-year groups 
after me than I expected.</i>

00:08.610 --> 00:10.660
<i>I should try to avoid conflict,</i>

00:10.660 --> 00:12.360
<i>even if it means ignoring 
designated areas.</i>

00:15.380 --> 00:20.410
<i>If Ayanokoji-senpai has to keep taking 
detours to avoid the first-years,</i>

00:21.010 --> 00:22.990
<i>we can win without ever making contact.</i>

00:24.950 --> 00:26.960
He's changed course.

00:26.960 --> 00:29.650
Groups in C4, move north.

00:29.650 --> 00:30.670
<i>Yes, ma'am.</i>

00:35.500 --> 00:36.930
I thought so.

00:37.530 --> 00:39.070
What is it, Tsubaki-san?

00:39.420 --> 00:43.170
The groups in C4 should be 
moving north, but they aren't.

00:43.530 --> 00:46.360
The same for the groups in B5.

00:48.290 --> 00:49.560
<i>What's the matter?</i>

00:49.560 --> 00:51.070
<i>What's happened?</i>

00:52.330 --> 00:53.810
<i>Will someone answer me?</i>

01:09.590 --> 01:15.390
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:19.470 --> 02:26.020
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:32.090 --> 02:34.510
<b>#15 Power and Will</b>

02:32.590 --> 02:36.550
The five first-year groups 
I sent aren't moving.

02:36.910 --> 02:41.390
There's a second-year group 
sticking close to each of them.

02:41.660 --> 02:45.510
It certainly looks like the second-years 
are blocking them, but...

02:45.510 --> 02:51.370
And it's an even distribution 
of students from all classes.

02:51.370 --> 02:56.150
You think someone's coordinating 
them, like you are for our groups?

02:57.110 --> 02:59.880
It appears our forces have 
reached their standby locations.

02:59.880 --> 03:01.410
Shall we begin?

03:01.410 --> 03:03.520
If you'd like.

03:03.520 --> 03:09.080
But how did you know we'd run into the 
first-year groups in the same areas?

03:11.920 --> 03:14.080
Over the past twelve days,

03:14.710 --> 03:19.840
the uninhabited island's terrain has 
seen subtle but very real changes.

03:20.690 --> 03:22.840
Do you know what those changes are?

03:23.260 --> 03:24.620
Changes in the terrain?

03:26.120 --> 03:29.680
Signs of travel, you mean?

03:30.290 --> 03:31.520
Yes.

03:31.840 --> 03:35.400
Students and teachers 
pass through every day.

03:35.910 --> 03:38.760
If you know where someone's going,

03:38.760 --> 03:41.950
it's not hard to determine what 
route they'll take to get there.

03:42.220 --> 03:46.450
So you can guess their path even if 
you're not actually watching them?

03:46.720 --> 03:51.270
Now, with designated areas and 
challenges currently active,

03:51.600 --> 03:54.210
who can we see standing still?

03:54.210 --> 03:59.450
Yagami Takuya-kun, Utomiya Riku-kun, 
Tsubaki Sakurako-san...

03:59.870 --> 04:03.060
Which of you is going head-to-head 
with me, pray tell?

04:03.470 --> 04:06.040
Or is it all three of you?

04:09.850 --> 04:11.980
Good evening, Ayanokoji-kun.

04:12.320 --> 04:14.230
How can I help you?

04:14.230 --> 04:17.730
I have something to ask of you.

04:17.990 --> 04:20.580
By all means, proceed.

04:20.580 --> 04:23.860
I must repay you for helping my classmate.

04:24.180 --> 04:26.370
It regards the White Room.

04:26.730 --> 04:30.580
I'm sure this will be quite 
a fascinating discussion.

04:34.120 --> 04:35.650
I see.

04:35.990 --> 04:40.040
So you'd like me to crush 
Amasawa Ichika-san, then?

04:40.360 --> 04:44.340
<i>No. It's about the first-year groups.</i>

04:44.340 --> 04:46.510
<i>I want you to handle them.</i>

04:46.750 --> 04:50.880
But it would be hard enough 
for a White Room student.

04:50.880 --> 04:55.890
I can't imagine anyone 
lesser pinning you down.

04:55.890 --> 04:58.760
The first-years will 
likely resort to force,

04:59.100 --> 05:02.400
blocking my approach to challenges 
and designated areas.

05:02.740 --> 05:04.730
I understand.

05:05.400 --> 05:08.120
You'll help me, then?

05:08.120 --> 05:13.200
But this is beyond what I owe 
you for helping Takemoto-kun.

05:13.560 --> 05:17.540
<i>You'll come out of this owing me a debt.</i>

05:17.900 --> 05:22.960
I don't love it, but if you get the 
job done, I accept that I'll owe you.

05:23.920 --> 05:25.370
You have a deal.

05:31.250 --> 05:36.480
Now, we've stopped those 
five suspicious groups.

05:36.850 --> 05:42.480
Let's see if we can track down 
the mastermind behind it all.

05:43.650 --> 05:44.990
Kito-kun?

05:45.910 --> 05:47.240
Um, Tsubaki-san...

05:47.650 --> 05:54.240
Is it that hard to direct the five groups 
to get away from the second-years?

05:54.500 --> 05:57.540
I'll explain when it's all over,

05:57.540 --> 06:00.040
but it's actually the opposite.

06:00.400 --> 06:06.260
They haven't pinned down my groups. 
I've pinned down theirs.

06:06.710 --> 06:08.000
You mean...

06:08.380 --> 06:12.650
Even if our five groups managed 
to corner Ayanokoji-senpai,

06:12.650 --> 06:15.890
his superior physicality would 
likely allow him to shake them off.

06:16.350 --> 06:20.900
But if we can't beat Ayanokoji-senpai, 
there's no point to this plan.

06:21.170 --> 06:24.080
There is a point. 
A far more important one.

06:24.080 --> 06:27.900
I've flushed out the 
groups protecting him.

06:29.410 --> 06:32.570
I don't know who's coordinating them,

06:32.570 --> 06:36.910
but I'll teach them that what they can 
see isn't the only thing that matters.

06:38.630 --> 06:41.280
<i>No one's left to get in your way.</i>

06:41.820 --> 06:44.420
<i>You can take this wherever you want to,</i>

06:44.880 --> 06:46.420
<i>Hosen-kun.</i>

06:46.420 --> 06:51.180
I found you, Ayanokoji-senpai!

06:54.550 --> 06:55.640
<i>It's Hosen.</i>

06:56.080 --> 06:57.640
<i>He didn't want our fight interrupted,</i>

06:57.860 --> 07:03.720
<i>so he told Nanase the day of the 
attack so we'd have time to prepare.</i>

07:04.030 --> 07:07.990
This is the moment I've been waiting for!

07:08.250 --> 07:12.240
I'm afraid I can't let 
you have that, Hosen.

07:13.660 --> 07:16.740
Get going, Ayanokoji.

07:17.120 --> 07:18.540
You're in the way.

07:21.600 --> 07:25.880
The hell are you doing here, Ryuen?

07:26.100 --> 07:28.750
I could ask you the same, Hosen.

07:29.070 --> 07:31.560
I can't imagine what 
business you'd have here.

07:31.950 --> 07:37.920
Eh? So you know what we're after?

07:38.710 --> 07:43.220
But it's none of your 
damn business what I do.

07:43.220 --> 07:46.520
Unfortunately, it is.

07:46.520 --> 07:49.780
I've been running low on 
funds lately, you see.

07:49.780 --> 07:51.880
I'm taking on mercenary work.

07:52.480 --> 07:54.030
So it's all about cash, huh?

07:54.990 --> 07:55.920
But that means...

07:56.340 --> 08:01.050
you actually think you can stop me?

08:01.050 --> 08:02.140
Does that mean...

08:02.140 --> 08:05.750
you think I <i>can't</i>?!

08:07.960 --> 08:10.130
You've still got a head like a rock.

08:13.940 --> 08:17.410
You didn't even last ten seconds, man.

08:17.410 --> 08:19.990
What a shitty joke!

08:31.040 --> 08:35.070
Yeah, I knew it. You're garbage at this.

08:35.630 --> 08:40.080
I doubt there's anyone out 
there you'd find satisfactory.

08:40.080 --> 08:41.910
Oh, but there is.

08:41.910 --> 08:47.080
Ayanokoji, the guy who 
went strolling past you.

08:47.360 --> 08:52.340
Ah, all right. So you know that, too?

08:52.570 --> 08:58.720
I've never met anyone who could 
block my punches that easily.

08:58.720 --> 09:03.650
And I don't think I'll ever see 
anyone else who could take a knife

09:03.650 --> 09:06.600
and look so composed!

09:07.060 --> 09:11.480
Sounds like you've been having 
some fun behind my back.

09:11.480 --> 09:15.620
So you're down bad for 
Ayanokoji, too, huh?!

09:18.100 --> 09:20.640
Yeah, I knew it, Ryuen!

09:20.640 --> 09:23.940
That's all you've got!

09:28.250 --> 09:31.250
Is that little whiffed 
punch all you were after?

09:31.250 --> 09:33.990
I'll kill you, damn it!

09:38.470 --> 09:41.700
The body can't hide it, right?

09:41.700 --> 09:46.640
Just accept that you're screwed already.

09:48.510 --> 09:50.570
Later, Ryuen.

09:50.570 --> 09:54.460
You were never worth my time.

09:54.460 --> 09:56.040
Hold it.

09:57.800 --> 10:01.220
What makes you think you've won?

10:02.220 --> 10:06.080
This sure as hell ain't over.

10:09.500 --> 10:12.400
Are you kidding me?

10:12.400 --> 10:14.760
It's taking all you've got 
just to stay on your feet.

10:14.980 --> 10:17.080
What's the point of hanging in there?

10:20.990 --> 10:22.850
What the hell are you—

10:27.330 --> 10:29.020
Screw this!

10:29.360 --> 10:33.220
Three-on-one was your plan, huh?!

10:33.220 --> 10:36.780
Quit your howling, gorilla man.

10:37.930 --> 10:39.680
You think you're pretty hot, huh?

10:39.680 --> 10:43.780
You can't even take me 
one-on-one, chicken shit!

10:44.210 --> 10:46.010
What a joke.

10:46.010 --> 10:51.210
What kind of moron would go 
one-on-one with a gorilla?!

10:58.420 --> 10:59.550
You—

11:09.040 --> 11:10.930
It's like hitting a rock.

11:10.930 --> 11:14.230
I'm hurting my own hands here.

11:14.230 --> 11:18.470
You haven't won, Ryuen!

11:19.490 --> 11:23.200
Doesn't matter to me how I get there.

11:23.200 --> 11:26.820
The last man standing is the winner.

11:26.820 --> 11:30.970
Next time we meet, you're dead...

11:31.690 --> 11:34.450
I'm not down for a rematch,

11:35.030 --> 11:39.510
but if you try to beat my ass 
and get yourself expelled...

11:40.260 --> 11:42.820
That'll make you the loser.

11:43.900 --> 11:45.650
Shut the hell—

11:51.370 --> 11:54.150
That was a hell of a brawl.

11:54.680 --> 11:57.420
Man, that guy's something else.

11:57.420 --> 12:00.200
He looked like a real 
monster for a sec there.

12:00.550 --> 12:02.900
Good work, you two.

12:03.220 --> 12:06.270
You'd better get going before 
the teachers show up.

12:07.160 --> 12:09.620
What about you?

12:09.930 --> 12:12.950
I'll be dropping out with Hosen.

12:14.070 --> 12:16.170
You sure about that?

12:17.730 --> 12:21.820
I've given Katsuragi everything he needs.

12:21.820 --> 12:25.570
Though we'll be unlikely to make 
it to the top three like this.

12:25.570 --> 12:27.990
That's too bad.

12:30.050 --> 12:33.600
Nah. I wouldn't say that.

12:35.560 --> 12:37.200
Thank you for the report.

12:37.200 --> 12:39.400
You can go back to the test.

12:39.630 --> 12:41.850
It didn't go the way you had hoped?

12:41.850 --> 12:44.300
He ended up in a brawl with 
a second-year named Ryuen,

12:44.300 --> 12:46.280
and they both got beat to hell.

12:46.680 --> 12:50.660
But we can still get Ayanokoji-senpai 
out of the running, right?

12:51.070 --> 12:55.330
It's no longer worth the risk.

12:56.360 --> 12:59.290
So we're backing off?

12:59.510 --> 13:02.050
I'm pretty unhappy.

13:02.050 --> 13:06.430
News of the bounty has 
taken on a life of its own,

13:06.660 --> 13:07.700
and most of all,

13:07.700 --> 13:11.380
my lack of trust in the other first-years

13:11.730 --> 13:14.770
made this plan a tough 
sell from the start.

13:14.770 --> 13:18.180
I'm starting to wish I'd 
done it all by myself.

13:20.890 --> 13:22.270
Where's Utomiya-kun?

13:22.880 --> 13:25.750
He was right here a minute ago...

13:28.570 --> 13:31.720
<b>Kito Hayato</b>

13:28.570 --> 13:31.720
<b>Utomiya Riku</b>

13:29.050 --> 13:30.500
What's he doing?

13:32.030 --> 13:36.710
You're Kito Hayato-senpai of Class 2-A.

13:37.270 --> 13:40.210
Sorry, but I can't let you past me.

13:40.480 --> 13:42.170
What's the big idea?

13:44.220 --> 13:46.300
Who sent you here?

13:46.650 --> 13:49.220
I won't hold back, 
even against an upperclassman.

13:56.690 --> 13:59.190
<i>Utomiya-kun? What are you doing?</i>

14:01.150 --> 14:03.900
<i>I thought you were taking orders from me.</i>

14:06.280 --> 14:08.320
I have what I came here for.

14:10.020 --> 14:11.340
<i>Utomiya-kun?</i>

14:12.250 --> 14:12.990
It's me.

14:13.500 --> 14:16.040
<i>Are you okay? What's Kito-senpai doing?</i>

14:16.040 --> 14:18.370
He just left.

14:18.370 --> 14:20.580
Why did you run off like that?

14:20.860 --> 14:25.590
Sorry. I wanted to stop him 
before he made it to you.

14:25.890 --> 14:28.290
If you can come back now, do so.

14:36.160 --> 14:41.580
<b>Last Day of the Test</b>

14:36.160 --> 14:41.580
<b>Last Day of the Test</b>

14:39.160 --> 14:41.610
<i>Good morning, Ayanokoji-kun.</i>

14:41.610 --> 14:44.610
<i>Yesterday was quite eventful, wasn't it?</i>

14:44.610 --> 14:47.360
You really saved my neck.

14:47.670 --> 14:49.660
The penalties weren't so bad?

14:49.980 --> 14:53.120
I see you moved a lot overnight.

14:53.120 --> 14:56.230
My first designated area is H3.

14:56.230 --> 14:58.620
I don't have time to spare, 
but I think I'll make it.

14:58.620 --> 15:00.870
H3, you say?

15:01.250 --> 15:05.880
As it happens, Ichinose-san from my group 
went missing at daybreak this morning.

15:05.880 --> 15:07.480
An accident?

15:07.480 --> 15:10.130
<i>No, I think she's pursuing 
some kind of goal.</i>

15:10.130 --> 15:13.890
She had been acting strangely 
the last few days.

15:13.890 --> 15:16.300
But why tell me that?

15:16.300 --> 15:19.960
<i>I've noticed she's in E3, as you are.</i>

15:20.530 --> 15:23.400
<i>Though she's on the 
opposite side, near D3.</i>

15:23.400 --> 15:27.120
What was your last 
designated area yesterday?

15:27.120 --> 15:28.400
<i>D5.</i>

15:28.940 --> 15:32.900
This morning, I realized our group 
points had gone down by one.

15:33.300 --> 15:36.840
Ichinose-san must have used a GPS search.

15:37.410 --> 15:40.910
It seems likely that she 
went to meet someone.

15:40.910 --> 15:44.670
<i>I can't think of another reason 
she'd head out so early.</i>

15:44.670 --> 15:49.170
<i>I thought perhaps she'd gone to see you.</i>

15:49.170 --> 15:51.550
I can't imagine why she would.

15:51.550 --> 15:52.760
What are you going to do?

15:52.760 --> 15:55.660
<i>We won't be able to claim 
arrival order rewards,</i>

15:55.660 --> 15:57.550
<i>but we'll just have to let her go.</i>

15:58.280 --> 16:00.780
Even if she ends up dropping out,

16:00.780 --> 16:04.430
as this is the last day, 
it shouldn't impact us too badly.

16:05.160 --> 16:09.080
<i>It's surprising behavior from 
a team player like Ichinose.</i>

16:09.080 --> 16:10.950
<i>It must be hard on you.</i>

16:10.950 --> 16:13.200
Accidents do happen.

16:13.800 --> 16:17.330
<i>If you happen to run into her, 
see if you can find out what she's up to.</i>

16:17.330 --> 16:18.290
<i>Goodbye.</i>

16:21.960 --> 16:26.730
<i>That's the patrol boat meant to pick 
up students after the test is over.</i>

16:28.430 --> 16:32.870
<i>Still, I2 is at the island's 
far northeast corner...</i>

16:33.330 --> 16:37.440
<i>At 3 PM, with so little time 
left before the test ends,</i>

16:37.440 --> 16:40.050
<i>it's an inconvenient choice 
for a designated area.</i>

16:40.720 --> 16:42.000
Ayanokoji-kun!

16:43.420 --> 16:44.610
Ichinose.

16:45.180 --> 16:47.230
You came all the way out here?

16:47.230 --> 16:53.360
I... I had to... see you.

16:53.810 --> 16:56.490
I... I'm on my way!

16:58.620 --> 17:00.810
I finally... caught up to you.

17:01.590 --> 17:04.290
What's going on here, Ichinose?

17:04.290 --> 17:10.080
I... I had to tell you something.

17:11.180 --> 17:12.800
What is it?

17:12.800 --> 17:17.790
My watch broke, and I was heading 
back to the starting point.

17:18.200 --> 17:22.500
On the way, I ran into Acting Chairman 
Tsukishiro and Shiba-sensei.

17:22.950 --> 17:25.760
They said that if you were still 
in the game on the final day,

17:25.760 --> 17:28.940
they'd lure you out to 
I2 and sabotage you.

17:28.940 --> 17:34.900
They said that if I told you, 
they'd get my classmates expelled...

17:35.470 --> 17:39.160
but I couldn't just let 
them do this to you!

17:39.850 --> 17:42.040
You should have, though.

17:42.040 --> 17:44.430
I'm your enemy, after all.

17:44.430 --> 17:45.580
I couldn't!

17:46.130 --> 17:48.710
You're not my enemy at all!

17:48.710 --> 17:49.850
Because...

17:50.340 --> 17:52.610
Because, Ayanokoji-kun...

17:53.200 --> 17:54.460
I love you!

17:55.970 --> 17:57.750
I-I mean...

17:58.160 --> 18:01.500
I didn't mean... I don't know why I...

18:03.100 --> 18:04.610
Thank you, Ichinose.

18:05.150 --> 18:09.290
I don't know what would have 
happened if you hadn't warned me.

18:09.720 --> 18:12.980
But I'm still heading to I2.

18:12.980 --> 18:15.240
You can't! It's not safe!

18:15.240 --> 18:19.990
You'll lose your precious 
classmates if I don't.

18:21.990 --> 18:25.390
Is what you said just now true?

18:25.390 --> 18:29.300
If it wasn't, you should deny it now. 
I don't want to get the wrong idea.

18:29.300 --> 18:33.380
Um... you didn't get the wrong idea.

18:33.790 --> 18:36.380
I do... love you.

18:37.520 --> 18:41.810
I think I only just realized it.

18:41.810 --> 18:48.770
To be honest, I'm a bit surprised 
to hear you felt that way.

18:49.680 --> 18:52.850
I'm sorry. I'm sure you don't like it.

18:53.170 --> 18:54.770
That's not true.

18:55.130 --> 18:59.280
But there are many things 
I have to take care of.

18:59.930 --> 19:04.120
I can't give you a clear yes 
or no answer until I do.

19:04.660 --> 19:08.750
That's the most honest answer 
I can give you right now.

19:10.290 --> 19:11.250
Okay.

19:14.230 --> 19:16.680
Hey there, Ayanokoji.

19:16.680 --> 19:18.170
Isn't this a coincidence?

19:18.470 --> 19:21.830
What brings you here, President Nagumo?

19:21.830 --> 19:23.180
I could ask you the same thing.

19:23.180 --> 19:26.840
There's neither a designated 
area nor a challenge nearby.

19:26.840 --> 19:28.680
Were you meeting up with Honami?

19:29.070 --> 19:31.210
Would there be a problem if I was?

19:31.210 --> 19:32.370
Not at all.

19:32.370 --> 19:37.320
But since you're still here without her, 
you must have had some other reason.

19:37.700 --> 19:41.440
I was just hoping we could 
have a conversation.

19:42.110 --> 19:46.950
You know about the 20-million-point 
bounty for having me expelled,

19:47.260 --> 19:52.220
and the fact that the first-years 
attacked me, correct?

19:52.220 --> 19:55.740
Don't blame me for that. 
It wasn't my idea.

19:56.190 --> 19:58.740
It was Acting Chairman 
Tsukishiro's, right?

19:59.090 --> 20:03.840
I wouldn't have gone along if the 
target were any other student,

20:04.260 --> 20:08.590
but you're the one man that 
Horikita-senpai thought highly of.

20:08.590 --> 20:13.100
I wanted to go toe-to-toe with 
you and see what you can do.

20:13.420 --> 20:15.800
I'm afraid I won't give 
you much of a fight.

20:15.800 --> 20:17.620
You don't really mean that.

20:18.340 --> 20:20.870
Your current ranking is 11.

20:21.220 --> 20:25.240
Well... maybe it's down to 15 or 16 now.

20:25.620 --> 20:26.990
True enough.

20:26.990 --> 20:29.290
I knew that if you 
really had hidden talent,

20:29.290 --> 20:31.560
you'd keep just under the radar,

20:31.560 --> 20:35.500
ready to spring to the top at any time.

20:36.120 --> 20:41.640
I spent a long time wondering 
what Horikita-senpai saw in you,

20:41.640 --> 20:43.880
but now I see it's justified.

20:44.780 --> 20:48.760
You've earned the right 
to be crushed by me.

20:49.050 --> 20:50.390
You should be pleased.

20:50.390 --> 20:54.200
I'm sorry, but I'm in a hurry.

20:54.200 --> 20:56.820
Can we finish this another time?

20:56.820 --> 20:59.650
What do you expect to find in I2?

20:59.650 --> 21:03.900
I'm not letting you go until 
you agree to fight me.

21:04.480 --> 21:05.780
If you want to—

21:07.470 --> 21:09.280
President Nagumo,

21:09.280 --> 21:12.950
despite everything, 
I hold you in high esteem.

21:13.390 --> 21:16.900
You have different talents 
than President Horikita,

21:16.900 --> 21:19.550
and you've risen brilliantly 
to the top of this school.

21:20.090 --> 21:24.690
But there are things you should 
leave well enough alone.

21:25.020 --> 21:26.720
Please leave now.

21:28.060 --> 21:31.730
You're giving me orders? 
Who the hell do you think you—

21:32.920 --> 21:35.740
I told you to leave. 
Do you understand me?

21:37.870 --> 21:39.730
<i>It went well, Nagumo.</i>

21:39.950 --> 21:42.480
<i>What are your next orders to delay Koenji?</i>

21:43.180 --> 21:44.800
<i>H-Hey, Nagumo?</i>

21:44.800 --> 21:46.440
Shouldn't you answer that?

21:50.490 --> 21:53.010
I'm taking you down!

21:53.010 --> 21:56.210
It will be my last job as 
student council president!

21:56.640 --> 21:57.600
I—

22:00.040 --> 22:03.050
A...yano...ko...
